WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.300
Hi, I'm Wasabi!

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.656
Agent training is simple: act, check, reward.

00:00:04.656 --> 00:00:06.675
The hard part is the check.

00:00:06.675 --> 00:00:08.695
Here's how Prime Intellect scales it.

00:00:10.475 --> 00:00:15.237
Twenty-three tasksets, one contract: a prebuilt sandbox per task, grading hidden until

00:00:15.237 --> 00:00:19.602
scoring, and a gold and no-op check before anything is trusted.

00:00:21.292 --> 00:00:24.468
Verifiers v1 splits an environment into three layers.

00:00:24.468 --> 00:00:27.247
The taskset holds the data and scoring.

00:00:27.247 --> 00:00:29.628
All twenty-three load through one API.

00:00:30.048 --> 00:00:33.871
The harness drives the agent; the runtime is where it runs.

00:00:33.871 --> 00:00:36.651
Any taskset, any harness, any runtime, one command.

00:00:38.525 --> 00:00:41.814
Every rollout walks the same hooks, with the agent sharing a

00:00:41.814 --> 00:00:43.011
sandbox with its grader.

00:00:43.431 --> 00:00:45.443
Setup boots the task's prebuilt image.

00:00:46.362 --> 00:00:50.786
The agent works with the grader hidden, since anything readable invites a reward hack.

00:00:51.206 --> 00:00:52.710
Finalize captures its diff.

00:00:53.915 --> 00:00:57.168
Then the tests are restored, and the taskset's own grader scores it.

00:00:58.675 --> 00:01:02.484
Before a taskset is trusted, its gold patch must pass the full

00:01:02.484 --> 00:01:05.340
scoring path, with failures retried up to ten times.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.003
Then a no-edit run.

00:01:07.003 --> 00:01:10.732
A task solved without any work is reward-hack fuel, so it's dropped,

00:01:10.732 --> 00:01:11.975
and kept for audit.

00:01:12.395 --> 00:01:15.373
For the noisiest sources, most rows don't survive.

00:01:15.373 --> 00:01:16.862
One loses eighty percent.

00:01:18.525 --> 00:01:21.832
Code has a fact to check: a hidden test passes, or it doesn't.

00:01:22.698 --> 00:01:25.204
The watercolour environment has no gold patch.

00:01:25.204 --> 00:01:28.425
Past an honesty gate, judge models score each painting.

00:01:29.808 --> 00:01:35.446
Agentic RL fails on thousands of tiny reward bugs, so treat environments

00:01:35.446 --> 00:01:37.326
as manufactured, validated artifacts.

00:01:39.192 --> 00:01:43.265
To recap: three layers, grading hidden until scoring, and a gold and

00:01:43.265 --> 00:01:44.962
no-op gate on every task.

00:01:45.382 --> 00:01:47.516
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:47.516 --> 00:01:48.126
I'm Wasabi.

00:01:48.126 --> 00:01:48.431
Bye!
